        "original_id": "f446c909-8b88-5828-aedf-2c701320d534",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lionel Hollins, Mike Fratello, Pete Maravich\n- Teams: Memphis Grizzlies, Brooklyn Nets, Philadelphia 76ers, Portland Trail Blazers, Boston Celtics\n- Roles: head coach, guard, TNT analyst\n- Seasons: 1979–80 Philadelphia 76ers season, 2004–05 Memphis Grizzlies season, 2004–05 NBA season\n\nFacts:\n- During the 1979–80 Philadelphia 76ers season, the Philadelphia 76ers acquired guard Lionel Hollins from the Portland Trail Blazers after Pete Maravich signed with the Boston Celtics.\n- The 2004–05 NBA season was the Memphis Grizzlies' tenth season in the National Basketball Association and their fourth season in Memphis.\n- During the 2004–05 Memphis Grizzlies season, the Memphis Grizzlies lost four straight games under Lionel Hollins before replacing him with TNT analyst Mike Fratello.\n- Lionel Hollins most recently served as the head coach of the Brooklyn Nets in the National Basketball Association.",
